  {
   "id": "g-notes-programRequirements",
   "label": "Additional program requirements",
   "category": "Liberal ed",
   "sourceRef": "program",
   "rule": {
    "id": "r-notes-programRequirements",
    "type": "review",
    "sourceRef": "program",
    "message": "All degree-seeking students must complete the University's\u00a0 Liberal Education requirements .\nAll freshmen in the College of Science and Engineering must complete CSE 1001: First-Year Experience.\n\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0 In addition to the core courses, students must select one of six sub-plans and complete the respective additional programmatic requirements (47-53 credits).\n-\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Professional\n-\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Biological\n-\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Computational\n-\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Secondary Education\n-\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Engineering\n- Integrated Bachelor of Science in Physics and Master of Science in Mechanical Engineering\n\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0 These requirements are subject to departmental review for each student.\n\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0 A sub-plan must be declared during the first semester after admission to the program.\n\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0 Students intending to pursue graduate study in physics are strongly encouraged to take PHYS 4303.\n\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0 At least half of the upper division credits within the major (19) must be taken at the University of Minnesota Twin Cities Campus.\nView\u00a0 Four-year Plans \u00a0for the College of Science and Engineering. Verify this requirement with your advisor or APAS."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "g-notes-programAdmissionRequirements",
   "label": "Program admission requirements",
   "category": "Major core",
   "sourceRef": "program",
   "rule": {
    "id": "r-notes-programAdmissionRequirements",
    "type": "review",
    "sourceRef": "program",
    "message": "Core Courses\nAll of the sub-plans start with a common foundation in physics and mathematics. This basic core of physics and math, taken during the first two years, provides the necessary tools to move into one of the sub-plans within physics.\nThe freshman and sophomore years give students a broad introduction to the fundamental ideas of physics. During this same period students learn the mathematical techniques that they will need for advanced work in physics and other sciences. Verify this requirement with your advisor or APAS."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "g-sub-plans",
   "label": "Sub-plan requirements",
   "category": "Major core",
   "sourceRef": "program",
   "rule": {
    "id": "r-sub-plans",
    "type": "review",
    "sourceRef": "program",
    "message": "Complete any sub-plan requirements that apply to you: Professional, Biological, Computational, Secondary Education, Engineering, Integrated Bachelor of Science in Physics and Master of Science in Mechanical Engineering. Verify this requirement with your advisor or APAS."
   }
  }
